{"term":"FKK","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"freikörperkultur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":5,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Abbreviation for Freikörperkultur ('Free Body Culture'), the organized German naturist movement promoting communal non-sexual nudity in designated outdoor and recreational spaces.","english_term":"naturism / FKK culture","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Culturally iconic in German-speaking countries; especially prominent in former East Germany where it was near-universal. More mainstream and desexualized than comparable nudist movements in Anglophone cultures."}
{"term":"FKK-Strand","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"nudist_beach","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":5,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A designated beach where nudity is permitted or customary within the Freikörperkultur tradition.","english_term":"nudist beach / FKK beach","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Common throughout Germany, Austria, and Scandinavia; usually signposted. Not considered taboo or sexual in mainstream German culture."}
{"term":"FKK-Verein","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"nudist_club","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":5,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"An organized club or association for the practice of Freikörperkultur, with membership, dedicated facilities, and designated grounds.","english_term":"nudist club / naturist association","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Reflects German Vereinskultur (associational club culture); many FKK-Vereine date to the early 20th century and were formalized or revived post-WWII."}
{"term":"Naturismus","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"naturism_practice","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":5,"technical":25,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Naturism: the philosophy and practice of communal nudity in natural settings as a wholesome, non-sexual lifestyle emphasizing connection with nature and bodily acceptance.","english_term":"naturism","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"More philosophical register than FKK or Nudismus; emphasizes the back-to-nature and health ideology. Affiliated internationally with the International Naturist Federation."}
{"term":"Naturist","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"naturism_practice","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":5,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A naturist; a person who practices and advocates for naturism as a lifestyle.","english_term":"naturist","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Loanword from English/French naturiste; carries slightly more philosophical connotation than Nudist."}
{"term":"Nudismus","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"nudism","concept":"naturism_practice","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":8,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Nudism: the practice of communal social nudity; used interchangeably with Naturismus but with a more pragmatic and less philosophical emphasis.","english_term":"nudism","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Nudismus vs. Naturismus: Nudismus refers to the practice itself; Naturismus implies the broader philosophical back-to-nature ideology. Both are non-sexual lifestyle terms."}
{"term":"Nudist","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"nudism","concept":"naturism_practice","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":8,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A nudist; a person who practices nudism by participating in communal social nudity.","english_term":"nudist","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Loanword from English 'nudist'; standard contemporary German usage."}
{"term":"Nacktbaden","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"nudism","concept":"nude_bathing","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":10,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Nude bathing; the act of bathing or swimming without clothing, typically at a designated beach or body of water.","english_term":"nude bathing / skinny dipping","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Highly normalized German compound noun; culturally routine rather than transgressive. Differs from English 'skinny dipping' in that it implies organized or designated-area practice rather than spontaneous activity."}
{"term":"Nacktcamping","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"nudism","concept":"nude_camping","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":8,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Nude camping; camping at designated naturist campsites where clothing is optional or not worn.","english_term":"nude camping / naturist camping","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Compound following standard German pattern; less universal than Nacktbaden but readily understood."}
{"term":"Nacktkultur","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"freikörperkultur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":8,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Nude culture; the broader cultural movement and lifestyle centered on communal social nudity, encompassing FKK and naturism as expressions of a body-positive worldview.","english_term":"nude culture / body culture","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Older or more literary variant of Freikörperkultur; can also refer broadly to a society's cultural attitudes toward the naked body rather than specifically to the FKK movement."}
{"term":"Nacktheit","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"nudity","concept":"nudity_state","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":12,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Nakedness; the state of being without clothing, applicable across neutral, artistic, medical, and sexual contexts.","english_term":"nakedness / nudity","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Semantically neutral; context determines whether the charge is clinical, aesthetic, or erotic. Core everyday German vocabulary with no inherent vulgarity."}
{"term":"Nacktbadestrand","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"nudist_beach","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":8,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A beach designated for nude bathing; a naturist beach.","english_term":"nude beach / naturist beach","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"More descriptively transparent compound than FKK-Strand (Nacktbaden + Strand); functionally synonymous but more explicit to audiences unfamiliar with the FKK abbreviation."}
{"term":"Freiluft-Nudismus","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"naturism","concept":"naturism_practice","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":8,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":60,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Open-air nudism; naturism practiced specifically in outdoor environments rather than enclosed or indoor venues.","english_term":"outdoor nudism / open-air naturism","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Compound of Freiluft (open air/outdoors) + Nudismus; emphasizes the outdoor dimension explicitly. Less common as a standalone term; more likely in advocacy, legal, or documentation contexts than in everyday speech."}
{"term":"Sexualaufklärung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_education","concept":"sex_education_talk","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":60,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual enlightenment or sex education; the formal or informal provision of accurate information about human sexuality, reproduction, and relationships to children, adolescents, or the public.","english_term":"sex education","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Carries the philosophical weight of Aufklärung (Enlightenment); frames sex education as rational emancipation from ignorance. Broader than the parental 'talk'; includes school curricula and public health campaigns."}
{"term":"Aufklärung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_education","concept":"sex_education_talk","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":3,"technical":40,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"In the context of sexuality, the act of informing a child or young person about sex, reproduction, and relationships; derived from the broader philosophical meaning of 'enlightenment' or 'clarification.'","english_term":"the birds and the bees talk / sex ed","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primary meaning is the 18th-century Enlightenment philosophical movement or generic clarification/briefing; sexual education sense is idiomatic and universally understood. German parents 'klären auf' (enlighten) their children about sex."}
{"term":"Sexualerziehung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_education","concept":"sex_education_talk","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":65,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual education; formal educational instruction covering biological, emotional, and relational aspects of sexuality as implemented in school curricula.","english_term":"sex education","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Erziehung = upbringing/education (broader than Unterricht/teaching). Standard term in German educational policy and school law. More systemic and formal than Aufklärung."}
{"term":"Sexualpädagogik","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_education","concept":"sex_education_talk","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":3,"technical":82,"recognition_pct_current":68,"recognition_pct_peak":72,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual pedagogy; the academic discipline and professional practice concerned with education and guidance around sexual development across the lifespan.","english_term":"sexual pedagogy / sex education","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"University and professional register; used in educator and social worker training. More specialized than Sexualerziehung; implies a theoretically grounded, lifespan-oriented discipline rather than just school curricula."}
{"term":"Sexualkunde","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"euphemisms_idioms","subcategory":"sex_education","concept":"sex_education_talk","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":58,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":94,"peak_year":1985,"regional":null,"definition":"Sex education as a designated school subject; the biology and health curriculum covering human reproduction, anatomy, and sexuality in German secondary schools.","english_term":"sex ed (school subject)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Specifically the named school subject (Sexualkunde-Unterricht). Somewhat dated; modern curricula may integrate content into Biologie or use Sexualerziehung. Strongly associated with generations schooled in the 1970s–2000s."}
{"term":"Schamgrenzen","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"shame_boundary","concept":"shame_threshold","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":58,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Shame thresholds or shame limits; the individual or culturally defined points at which bodily exposure, nudity, or sexual behavior triggers a shame response.","english_term":"shame thresholds / shame limits","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Key term in German Sexualpädagogik; used to describe where individual modesty begins and what triggers shame. Recognizing and respecting Schamgrenzen is a central ethical principle in German sex education curricula."}
{"term":"Schamgefühl","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"shame","concept":"sexual_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":50,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The sense or feeling of shame; in sexual contexts, the emotional experience of embarrassment, exposure, or violation when one's body or sexuality is involved.","english_term":"sense of shame / shame response","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Not exclusively sexual; core psychological vocabulary. In sex education, Schamgefühl is treated as a natural emotional response to be acknowledged and respected rather than dismissed, forming the basis for boundary-setting education."}
{"term":"Intimitätsgrenzen","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"intimacy_boundary","concept":"intimacy_boundaries","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":3,"technical":62,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Intimacy limits or personal boundaries; the lines an individual draws around physical closeness, touch, and sexual contact with others.","english_term":"intimacy limits / personal boundaries","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Standard term in German sexual health education, therapy, and consent education. Often taught alongside Zustimmung and Grenzüberschreitung in school-based programs."}
{"term":"Grenzüberschreitung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"boundary_violation","concept":"consent_violation","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":10,"technical":55,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Boundary violation or transgression; in sexual contexts, the act of crossing another person's stated or implied bodily, intimate, or sexual limits without consent.","english_term":"boundary violation / transgression","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"General German compound for crossing any limit (border crossing, rule breaking, personal boundary); in sexual and pedagogical discourse specifically denotes unwanted physical or intimate contact. Severity ranges from mild to criminal."}
{"term":"Zustimmung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"consent","concept":"sexual_consent","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":3,"technical":60,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Consent or agreement; in sexual contexts, the freely given, informed, and ongoing agreement to engage in sexual activity.","english_term":"consent","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"General German word for agreement/approval across all domains; in sexual discourse the standard lay and educational term for consent. Less formal than Einwilligung; more common in everyday sex education and activist language."}
{"term":"Einwilligung","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"consent","concept":"sexual_consent","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":3,"technical":72,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Informed consent; the formal or legal expression of voluntary agreement to a specific act including sexual contact; carries stronger legal weight than Zustimmung.","english_term":"informed consent","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Preferred legal and medical-ethical term; appears in German sexual assault legislation (§177 StGB) and medical ethics discourse. More formal register than Zustimmung; implies a specific, deliberate act of agreement rather than general willingness."}
{"term":"Konsens","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"consent","concept":"sexual_consent","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":3,"technical":50,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Mutual consent or consensus; in sexual discourse, the shared and ongoing agreement of all parties to engage in sexual activity, emphasizing its collaborative and negotiated character.","english_term":"consensus / consent","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From Latin consensus; used across political, academic, and social domains. In sexual discourse particularly prominent in BDSM and consent-culture communities ('Konsens-Prinzip') as well as mainstream sex education. Emphasizes mutuality more explicitly than Zustimmung or Einwilligung."}
